# Bill of Materials

This document lists the major hardware components associated with the Smart Sea Belt prototype.

## Smart Watch

| Component | Quantity | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| ESP32-C3 | 1 per wearable | Main controller and BLE |
| MAX30102 | 1 per wearable | Heart-rate sensing |
| MPU6050 | 1 per wearable | Motion sensing |
| SOS Button | 1 per wearable | Manual emergency activation |
| Buzzer | 1 per wearable | Local alert |
| Vibration/Indicator | 1 per wearable | User notification |
| Battery | 1 per wearable | Power supply |

## Boat Hub

| Component | Quantity | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| ESP32-S3 | 1 | Central controller |
| BLE interface | Integrated | Smart Watch communication |
| GPS / NavIC module | 1 | Location awareness |
| LoRa module | 1 | Long-range communication |
| Display | 1 | System status |
| Buzzer | 1 | Emergency alert |
| Rudder actuator/interface | 1 | Diversion mechanism |

## Base Unit

| Component | Quantity | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| Controller | 1 | Data processing |
| LoRa receiver/module | 1 | Boat Hub communication |
| Display | 1 | Monitoring |
| Buzzer | 1 | Emergency alert |
| Power supply | 1 | System power |

## Safety and Mechanical Components

| Component | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Flotation mechanism | Emergency buoyancy support |
| Marine protection/enclosure | Protection of electronics |
| Rudder actuator assembly | Controlled diversion mechanism |
| Wiring and connectors | Hardware integration |
| Mounting components | Mechanical assembly |

## Notes

The exact quantities and specifications should be updated according to the components physically used in the prototype.

This BOM is intended as a hardware documentation reference and should not be interpreted as a certified marine equipment specification.
